    "marks": 20,
    "model": "Owners are internal stakeholders who fund the business and take its main decisions, so their goals for profit and growth shape the strategy. A business that fails to meet their expectations may lose its investment or its leadership. Employees are also internal stakeholders, and their skills and motivation determine the quality of the product and the service, which affect sales. Suppliers are external stakeholders who provide the inputs the business needs, so reliable supply and fair terms allow production to continue on schedule. Consumers are external stakeholders who generate the revenue, and a loss of their trust reduces sales quickly. Each group depends on the others, so a problem with one affects the rest.",
    "prompt": "Explain the importance of two internal stakeholders and two external stakeholders to a named small Irish business.",
    "type": "short"
