  "questions": [
   {
    "marks": 25,
    "model": "Consider a reusable steel water bottle sold to students and office workers in Cork. Product: a durable bottle with a leak-proof lid, in a range of colours, with a warranty and a replacement lid service. Pricing: a mid-premium price, set above supermarket bottles to reflect durability, with a bundle offer for students. Promotion: social media and campus ambassadors who show the bottle in daily use, plus partnerships with cafes that offer a discount to customers who refill. People: staff trained to explain the warranty and the refill scheme. Packaging: recycled card packaging with a clear care guide, since the product is sold on sustainability. Process: online ordering with a simple returns process and fast delivery to student accommodation. Place: sold online, through campus shops and in selected sports stores. USP analysis: the uniqueness lies in the lifetime warranty and replacement lid service, which few rivals offer. Customer value is high, because students who replace cheap bottles often value a product that lasts. Defensibility is moderate: rivals can copy a warranty, but the firm can strengthen its position through the refill scheme and the brand's sustainability record.",
    "prompt": "Develop a full 7-P marketing mix for a product of your choice, and carry out a USP analysis for the product.",
    "type": "short"
   },
   {
    "marks": 15,
    "model": "Evaluation: the mix may fail the fit test if its promotion still reaches customers through channels they have stopped using, such as print advertising, while the target market now books online. The process may also be weak if booking requires a phone call, which deters younger customers. Consistency matters too: if the price is premium but the promotion uses frequent discounts, the message is confused. Improvement one: move promotion to social media and search advertising, measuring response rates, so spending is directed at the channels the target market uses. Improvement two: streamline the process by adding online booking with reminders, which saves time for customers and reduces missed appointments. Both changes address the weakest elements of the mix while keeping the price and brand intact.",
    "prompt": "Evaluate the marketing mix of a service business whose bookings are falling, and suggest two ways of improving it.",
    "type": "short"
   }
  ]
